      question: 'Explain the relationship between Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Deep Learning. Use examples for each and explain how they are connected to each other.',
      answer: 'Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and Deep Learning are three related concepts where each is a subset of the previous one. Artificial Intelligence (AI) is the broadest concept — it refers to any technique that makes machines intelligent, enabling them to think, learn, and act like humans. An example is a smart speaker that answers questions. Machine Learning is a specific method of achieving AI. Instead of programming rules manually, the machine is given data and learns the rules on its own. An example is image recognition — you show the system thousands of photos of cats and dogs and it learns to tell them apart. Deep Learning is a more advanced type of Machine Learning. It uses multiple layers of artificial neurons — inspired by the human brain — to learn very complex patterns. An example is self-driving cars, which must process road conditions, traffic signs, pedestrians, and other vehicles all at the same time. The relationship is like three concentric circles: AI is the largest circle containing all approaches to machine intelligence. Machine Learning is inside AI — a specific approach using data. Deep Learning is inside Machine Learning — using neural networks for the most complex tasks.',
