      answer: 'Every HTML page has four essential structure tags. First, the <html> tag — this is the most important tag. It wraps around the entire web page and tells the browser that everything inside it is HTML. Without it, the browser may not correctly read the document. Second, the <head> tag — this defines the header section of the page. Information in the head section is not displayed on screen — it contains information about the document, like the title and links to stylesheets. Third, the <title> tag — placed inside the head section, it gives the web page its title. This title appears on the browser tab at the top of the window. Fourth, the <body> tag — this is the main part of the HTML page. Everything that appears on the browser screen — all the text, images, links, tables — is placed inside the body tags. Here is a simple HTML page using all four: <html><head><title>My First Page</title></head><body>Welcome to the world of HTML. This is my first web page.</body></html>',
